### 38 cli query --help
$ wtf query --help --root <root> --now 2026-09-16T12:00:00-04:00
exit 0
--- stdout
Query tasks, values, tables, plans, resources and diagnostics

Usage: wtf query [OPTIONS] <FILE> <QUERY>
       wtf query [OPTIONS] --workspace <QUERY>

Arguments:
  <FILE_OR_QUERY>  A note relative to --root, or the query expression when --workspace is set
  [QUERY]          A functional expression or collection pipeline; use - for stdin

Options:
      --workspace      Query all indexed notes instead of supplying a positional note file
      --root <ROOT>    [default: .]
      --json           Emit a JSON array, preserving dates, currencies and units
      --jsonl          Emit one JSON value per line
      --on <ON>        Evaluate at local midnight on this date
      --now <NOW>      Freeze the clock and timezone offset using an RFC3339 timestamp
      --fail-on-match  Return exit status 1 if the query returns any rows (useful for diagnostics)
  -h, --help           Print help

Bindings: ast, graph, tasks, events, stops, entries, values, plans, tables, rows, resources, diagnostics, notes
Functions: map, filter, fold, get, sort_by, group_by, sum, length
Stages: where, select, sort, limit, count, sum, group
Use - as QUERY to read an expression from stdin.
Examples: wtf query note.wtf 'map(tasks, fn(t) => t.title)' --json
          wtf query --workspace 'filter(tasks, fn(t) => !t.done)' --json
          printf 'length(tasks)' | wtf query note.wtf -

